Generic single-database configuration.


# fresh deployments

At a certain point in the migration chain we create an `auth` schema that is
owned by Better Auth. Better Auth's CLI must run at that point — before the
later symbology migrations that reference `auth."user"` (the watchlist FK in
s8c9d0e1f2a3). So a straight `alembic upgrade head` fails on a fresh DB.

Use the automated bootstrap from the repo root (source of truth):

    just db-init

It sequences the three phases and is idempotent, so it also works as the
everyday migrate entrypoint on an existing DB.

If you need to run the phases by hand, it does the equivalent of:

    cd server && uv run alembic upgrade r7b8c9d0e1f2   # create auth schema
    cd ../ui  && npx @better-auth/cli migrate -y       # create auth."user", etc.
    cd ../server && uv run alembic upgrade head         # apply remaining migrations

The watchlist migration (s8c9d0e1f2a3) guards against running out of order: if
auth."user" is missing it raises an actionable error instead of a cryptic
`relation "auth.user" does not exist`.
